IMPORT prelude

-- Higher Education Support Act 2003 (Cth) -- HECS-HELP and FEE-HELP from the seat of the student who borrows and the
-- former student who repays.
--
-- SEAT: the student (and later the former student repaying) -- "What is deferred as a HELP debt, and when must I repay?"
-- Every exported question is phrased as that person would ask it. Where a provision addresses only the provider, the
-- Secretary or the Commissioner, it is encoded as what it means for the student: whether they can be told they are
-- Commonwealth supported, whether a balance is re-credited, what is collected after death.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Commonwealth supported student (ss 36-5, 36-10); HECS-HELP entitlement and amount (ss 90-1, 90-5,
-- 93-1, 93-10, 93-20, 96-1); FEE-HELP entitlement (ss 104-1, 104-5); the HELP balance, loan limit and re-crediting on
-- repayment (ss 128-15, 128-20, 128-25); HELP debts, the FEE-HELP loan fee, when a debt is incurred and the 20% cut
-- (ss 137-5, 137-10, 137-19A); discharge on death (ss 137-20, 140-40); the accumulated HELP debt and its indexation
-- (ss 140-5, 140-10, 140-25, 140-26, 140-30); voluntary repayment (ss 151-1, 151-10, 151-15); compulsory repayment
-- (ss 154-1, 154-5, 154-10, 154-15, 154-20, 154-25); the notice on leaving Australia (s 154-18(1)).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 104, compilation date 1 July 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 17, 2025), register id
-- C2026C00297, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A01234.txt. No regulation or guideline is deposited.
-- The repayment thresholds and the repayment rates are the Act's own (ss 154-10, 154-20); after 2025-26 they are indexed
-- under s 154-25; the AWE figures that index them are INPUTS. The text deposit drops the formulas the Register prints as
-- images (ss 93-5(1), 140-25(1), 140-26(2), 154-25(2)); they are transcribed by hand from the Word rendering of the same
-- compilation in ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A01234.formulas.md (2026-10-21) and encoded here.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Allocation of places and grant amounts (Divisions 30, 33) beyond what the Commonwealth supported test needs;
-- the Student Learning Entitlement itself, the academic-suitability assessment, the s 36-10(6), (7) and s 36-12 bars, the
-- FEE-HELP course requirements and the s 104-1(3), (4) and 104-1AA bars (all INPUTS: judgments or facts of the provider);
-- the student contribution amount itself (set by the provider within the maximum, s 19-87 -- an INPUT); grandfathered
-- students; indexation of the maximum contributions and the loan limit under Part 5-6 (the current figures are INPUTS; the
-- figures below are the ones the text states); CPI, WPI and AWE index numbers (INPUTS); re-crediting for special circumstances (Division 97, Subdivision 104-B); OS-HELP, SA-HELP,
-- STARTUP-HELP and VET FEE-HELP; the overseas debtors' levy (ss 154-16, 154-17, 154-32) and the Overseas Debtors Repayment
-- Guidelines (not deposited); location-preferred debtors (Divisions 142, 144); assessments, PAYG and recovery; s 8 of the
-- Medicare Levy Act 1986 and the tax-law components of repayment income (INPUTS); and every earlier text of the Act.
-- THIS IS THE 2026 TEXT: Daniel's 2014 and 2017 enrolments, and Chloe's 2024-25 repayment, were governed by texts that are
-- not deposited.
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers. An income year is named by the year in which it starts (2025 for 2025-26).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the student's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.

§ `Higher Education Support Act 2003 -- HELP loans and their repayment`

-- "permanent humanitarian visa holder", "eligible former permanent humanitarian visa holder" (one who no longer holds a
-- permanent humanitarian visa but did, and holds a visa of a determined class), "Pacific engagement visa holder" and
-- "permanent visa holder" are the Act's terms (Dictionary, Schedule 1). Which one a student is, is a fact they can state.
DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    `an Australian citizen`
    `a New Zealand citizen`
    `a permanent humanitarian visa holder`
    `an eligible former permanent humanitarian visa holder`
    `a Pacific engagement visa holder`
    `another permanent visa holder`
    `none of these`

-- The facts about one student's enrolment in one unit of study -- the Act's natural unit (a debt is incurred unit by unit,
-- at the unit's census date). Facts about the provider are ones the provider tells the student.
DECLARE Enrolment HAS
    `status` IS A Status
    `will be resident in Australia for the unit` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 90-5(2A)(b)-(e) / 104-5(2A)(b)-(e): the special category visa and residence-history test for New Zealanders
    `meets the New Zealand special category test` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- for an eligible former permanent humanitarian visa holder: whether the visa now held is a permanent visa
    `holds a permanent visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provider expects no units in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provider has a funding agreement for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Table A provider` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unit is within a funded national priority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unit contributes to the course` IS A BOOLEAN
    `assessed as academically suited` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unit is covered by the Student Learning Entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `FEE-FREE Uni Ready course` IS A BOOLEAN
    `enrolled at the end of the census date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `commenced the course on or after 1 January 2021` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has and notified a student identifier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another s 36-10 or 36-12 bar applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `advised in writing of Commonwealth support` IS A BOOLEAN
    `opted out in writing by the census date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Secretary determined not a genuine student` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accredited course` IS A BOOLEAN
    `census date` IS A NUMBER
    `HELP balance` IS A NUMBER
    `meets the tax file number requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave a request for Commonwealth assistance by the census date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `course is primarily at an overseas campus` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the FEE-HELP course requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a bar in s 104-1(3), (4) or 104-1AA applies` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `ss 36-5, 36-10 -- Am I a Commonwealth supported student`

-- s 36-10(1)(f), mirrored in s 104-1(1)(ga): the student identifier requirements apply "if: (i) the census date for the unit is
-- on or after 1 January 2021 and before 1 January 2023 and the person commenced the course of study on or after 1 January 2021;
-- or (ii) the census date for the unit is on or after 1 January 2023". (2C): the person "has a student identifier immediately
-- before the census date" and, before it, notifies it to the provider and the Secretary.
@export Do the student identifier requirements apply to my unit (s 36-10(1)(f))?
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment @desc The facts of your enrolment in the unit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the student identifier requirements apply to me` IF
        (    `the enrolment`'s `census date` AT LEAST 20210101
         AND `the enrolment`'s `census date` LESS THAN 20230101
         AND `the enrolment`'s `commenced the course on or after 1 January 2021`)
    OR  `the enrolment`'s `census date` AT LEAST 20230101

@export Do I meet the student identifier condition (ss 36-10(1)(f), 104-1(1)(ga))?
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment @desc The facts of your enrolment in the unit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the student identifier condition` IF
    (NOT `Do the student identifier requirements apply to me` `the enrolment`) OR `the enrolment`'s `has and notified a student identifier`

-- s 36-10(2): "(a) an Australian citizen; or (b) a citizen of New Zealand who will be resident within Australia for the
-- duration of the unit; or (c) a permanent visa holder who will be resident within Australia for the duration of the unit".
-- (2B): not if the provider "reasonably expects that he or she will not undertake in Australia any units of study contributing
-- to the course of study". INFERENCE: permanent humanitarian and Pacific engagement visas are permanent visas; an eligible
-- former permanent humanitarian visa holder counts only if the visa now held is a permanent visa (asked as a fact).
@export Do I meet the citizenship or residency requirements for a Commonwealth supported place (s 36-10(2))?
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment @desc The facts of your enrolment in the unit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the citizenship or residency requirements for a Commonwealth supported place` IF
        (NOT `the enrolment`'s `provider expects no units in Australia`)
    AND CONSIDER `the enrolment`'s `status`
        WHEN `an Australian citizen` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `an eligible former permanent humanitarian visa holder` THEN
            `the enrolment`'s `holds a permanent visa` AND `the enrolment`'s `will be resident in Australia for the unit`
        OTHERWISE `the enrolment`'s `will be resident in Australia for the unit`

-- s 36-10(1): "A higher education provider must not advise a person that he or she is a Commonwealth supported student in
-- relation to a unit of study unless: (a) the provider has entered into a funding agreement under section 30-25 for the year
-- ...; (b) the unit contributes to the requirements of a course of study in which the person is enrolled ...; (ba) the person
-- has been assessed ... as academically suited to undertake the unit; (c) the person meets the citizenship or residency
-- requirements ...; (d) if the course of study is a course of study other than a FEE-FREE Uni Ready course -- the unit is covered
-- by the person's Student Learning Entitlement; (e) the person enrolled in the unit on or before the census date ... and ...
-- remained so enrolled; (f) [student identifier]". (5): a provider that is not a Table A provider must not, unless the unit is
-- within a national priority for which it has received a grant. (6), (7) and s 36-12: further bars (one INPUT flag here).
@export Could my provider lawfully tell me I am Commonwealth supported for the unit (s 36-10)?
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment @desc The facts of your enrolment in the unit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Could my provider lawfully tell me I am Commonwealth supported` IF
        `the enrolment`'s `provider has a funding agreement for the year`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `unit contributes to the course`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `assessed as academically suited`
    AND `Do I meet the citizenship or residency requirements for a Commonwealth supported place` `the enrolment`
    AND (`the enrolment`'s `FEE-FREE Uni Ready course` OR `the enrolment`'s `unit is covered by the Student Learning Entitlement`)
    AND `the enrolment`'s `enrolled at the end of the census date`
    AND `Do I meet the student identifier condition` `the enrolment`
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `opted out in writing by the census date`)
    AND (`the enrolment`'s `Table A provider` OR `the enrolment`'s `unit is within a funded national priority`)
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `another s 36-10 or 36-12 bar applies`)

-- s 36-5(1): a person is a Commonwealth supported student in relation to a unit if "(a) the higher education provider ... has
-- advised the person in writing that he or she is a Commonwealth supported student ...; and (b) at the end of the census date
-- for the unit, the higher education provider would not have been prohibited under this Subdivision from so advising the person".
-- (3), (4): not if he or she notifies, in writing and on or before the census date, "that he or she does not wish to be";
-- (5): nor if "the Secretary determines that the person is not a genuine student in relation to the unit" (asked as a fact).
-- Whether a postgraduate course carries Commonwealth supported places is not answered by the Act: it turns on the provider's
-- advice and funding agreement and, for a Table A provider, on the Minister's allocation of places (ss 30-10, 30-12) -- INPUTS.
@export Am I a Commonwealth supported student in the unit (s 36-5)?
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment @desc The facts of your enrolment in the unit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a Commonwealth supported student` IF
        `the enrolment`'s `advised in writing of Commonwealth support`
    AND `Could my provider lawfully tell me I am Commonwealth supported` `the enrolment`
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `opted out in writing by the census date`)
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `Secretary determined not a genuine student`)

§§ `ss 90-1, 90-5, 104-1, 104-5 -- Am I entitled to HECS-HELP or FEE-HELP`

-- s 90-5(1) and s 104-5(1): "(a) the student is an Australian citizen; or (b) the student: (i) is a permanent humanitarian visa
-- holder, an eligible former permanent humanitarian visa holder or a Pacific engagement visa holder; and (ii) will be resident in
-- Australia for the duration of the unit". (2A): certain New Zealand citizens resident in Australia who hold or held a special
-- category visa and meet the residence-history test. (3): not if the provider reasonably expects no units in Australia.
-- An ordinary permanent visa holder, who may be Commonwealth supported under s 36-10(2)(c), is NOT in this list.
-- (s 104-5(1)(c), permanent visa holders in a bridging course for overseas-trained professionals, is not encoded.)
@export Do I meet the citizenship or residency requirements for HECS-HELP and FEE-HELP (ss 90-5, 104-5)?
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment @desc The facts of your enrolment in the unit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the citizenship or residency requirements for a HELP loan` IF
        (NOT `the enrolment`'s `provider expects no units in Australia`)
    AND CONSIDER `the enrolment`'s `status`
        WHEN `an Australian citizen` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a permanent humanitarian visa holder` THEN `the enrolment`'s `will be resident in Australia for the unit`
        WHEN `an eligible former permanent humanitarian visa holder` THEN `the enrolment`'s `will be resident in Australia for the unit`
        WHEN `a Pacific engagement visa holder` THEN `the enrolment`'s `will be resident in Australia for the unit`
        WHEN `a New Zealand citizen` THEN
            `the enrolment`'s `will be resident in Australia for the unit` AND `the enrolment`'s `meets the New Zealand special category test`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 90-1: "A student is entitled to HECS-HELP assistance for a unit of study ... if: (aa) the course of study is an accredited
-- course ...; (a) the student meets the citizenship or residency requirements under section 90-5; (b) the census date for the unit
-- is on or after 1 January 2005; (ba) the student's HELP balance is greater than zero; (c) the student is a Commonwealth supported
-- student in relation to the unit; (e) the student (i) enrolled in the unit on or before the census date ... and (ii) at the end of
-- the census date, remained so enrolled; (f) the student meets the tax file number requirements ...; (g) the student has, on or
-- before the census date, completed, signed and given ... a request for Commonwealth assistance".
-- The census date is the date the provider fixes for the unit under s 169-25(1) (Dictionary, "census date").
@export Am I entitled to HECS-HELP assistance for the unit (s 90-1)?
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment @desc The facts of your enrolment in the unit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to HECS-HELP assistance` IF
        `the enrolment`'s `accredited course`
    AND `Do I meet the citizenship or residency requirements for a HELP loan` `the enrolment`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `census date` AT LEAST 20050101
    AND `the enrolment`'s `HELP balance` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `Am I a Commonwealth supported student` `the enrolment`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `enrolled at the end of the census date`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `meets the tax file number requirements`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `gave a request for Commonwealth assistance by the census date`

-- s 104-1(1): entitled if "(a) the student meets the citizenship or residency requirements under section 104-5; (ac) the student
-- has been assessed ... as academically suited ...; (b) the student's HELP balance is greater than zero; (c) the census date ...
-- is on or after 1 January 2005; (d) the student is not a Commonwealth supported student in relation to the unit; (e) the unit
-- meets the course requirements under section 104-10; (g) [enrolled at the census date]; (ga) [student identifier]; (h) [tax file
-- number]; (i) [request for Commonwealth assistance]". (1AA): not if the Secretary determines the student "is not a genuine
-- student"; (2): not if the course is undertaken "primarily at an overseas campus"; (3), (4) and s 104-1AA: further bars (one
-- INPUT flag).
@export Am I entitled to FEE-HELP assistance for the unit (s 104-1)?
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment @desc The facts of your enrolment in the unit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to FEE-HELP assistance` IF
        `Do I meet the citizenship or residency requirements for a HELP loan` `the enrolment`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `assessed as academically suited`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `HELP balance` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the enrolment`'s `census date` AT LEAST 20050101
    AND (NOT `Am I a Commonwealth supported student` `the enrolment`)
    AND `the enrolment`'s `meets the FEE-HELP course requirements`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `enrolled at the end of the census date`
    AND `Do I meet the student identifier condition` `the enrolment`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `meets the tax file number requirements`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `gave a request for Commonwealth assistance by the census date`
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `Secretary determined not a genuine student`)
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `course is primarily at an overseas campus`)
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `a bar in s 104-1(3), (4) or 104-1AA applies`)

§§ `ss 93-1, 93-5, 93-10, 93-20, 96-1 -- What is deferred`

-- s 93-5(1): "A person's student contribution amount for a unit of study is the amount worked out as follows:" -- formula
-- (sidecar): The person's student contribution amount for a place in the unit x The EFTSL value of the unit. (4): an amount
-- "made up of dollars and cents" is rounded "down to the nearest dollar". The amount for a place is the provider's (s 19-87(2)),
-- an INPUT; (3) (nil for a FEE-FREE Uni Ready course) is not encoded.
@export What is my student contribution amount for the unit (s 93-5(1), (4))?
GIVEN `student contribution amount for a place` IS A NUMBER @desc The student contribution amount the provider set for a place in the unit, in dollars
      `EFTSL value of the unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The unit's EFTSL value (a full-time year is 1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my student contribution amount for the unit` IS
    FLOOR (`student contribution amount for a place` TIMES `EFTSL value of the unit`)

-- s 93-1: the amount of HECS-HELP assistance for a unit "is the difference between: (a) his or her student contribution amount
-- for the unit; and (b) the sum of any up-front payments made in relation to the unit". s 93-20(1): if it would exceed the HELP
-- balance on the census date (and no other unit shares the census date), it is "an amount equal to the student's HELP balance".
-- s 96-1: the Commonwealth must "(a) as a benefit to the student, lend to the student the amount of HECS-HELP assistance; and
-- (b) pay to the provider the amount lent in discharge of the student's liability to pay his or her student contribution amount".
@export How much HECS-HELP assistance is lent to me for the unit (ss 93-1, 93-20(1))?
GIVEN `student contribution amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The student contribution amount the provider charges for the unit, in dollars
      `up-front payments` IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid up front towards it, in dollars
      `balance on the census date` IS A NUMBER @desc Your HELP balance on the unit's census date, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much HECS-HELP assistance do I get for the unit` IS
    min (max 0 (`student contribution amount` MINUS `up-front payments`)) `balance on the census date`

-- s 93-20(2): if the HECS-HELP, FEE-HELP and VET FEE-HELP amounts for all units with the same census date "would exceed the
-- student's HELP balance on the census date ..., the total amount ... is an amount equal to that HELP balance". The Act's
-- example: Kate, a HELP balance of $2,000, four units at $600 each -- $2,000.
@export How much HELP assistance do I get in total for units with the same census date (s 93-20(2))?
GIVEN `sum of the amounts for units with that census date` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the HELP amounts you would otherwise get for those units, in dollars
      `balance on the census date` IS A NUMBER @desc Your HELP balance on that census date, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much HELP assistance do I get for units with one census date` IS
    min `sum of the amounts for units with that census date` `balance on the census date`

-- s 93-10 table, "The amount in respect of a non-grandfathered student". Note 2: "Maximum student contribution amounts for places
-- are indexed under Part 5-6" -- so these are the figures the text states, not the figure for any particular year.
DECLARE `Funding cluster part` IS ONE OF
    `law, accounting, administration, economics or commerce`
    `communications or society and culture`
    `education, clinical psychology, English, mathematics or statistics`
    `allied or other health, built environment, computing, visual and performing arts, professional pathway psychology or social work`
    `nursing or Indigenous and foreign languages`
    `engineering, surveying, environmental studies or science`
    `agriculture`
    `medicine, dentistry or veterinary science`
    `pathology`

@export What is the most I can be charged for a Commonwealth supported place, as the s 93-10 table states it (before indexation)?
GIVEN `the discipline` IS A `Funding cluster part` @desc The discipline the unit falls in
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be charged for a place` IS
    CONSIDER `the discipline`
    WHEN `law, accounting, administration, economics or commerce` THEN 14500
    WHEN `communications or society and culture` THEN 14500
    WHEN `education, clinical psychology, English, mathematics or statistics` THEN 3950
    WHEN `allied or other health, built environment, computing, visual and performing arts, professional pathway psychology or social work` THEN 7950
    WHEN `nursing or Indigenous and foreign languages` THEN 3950
    WHEN `engineering, surveying, environmental studies or science` THEN 7950
    WHEN `agriculture` THEN 3950
    WHEN `medicine, dentistry or veterinary science` THEN 11300
    WHEN `pathology` THEN 7950

§§ `ss 128-15, 128-20, 128-25 -- How much can I still borrow`

-- s 128-20(1): "The HELP loan limit is: (a) $106,319; or (b) in relation to a person who is enrolled in a course of study in
-- medicine, ... dentistry, ... veterinary science or ... aviation, while the person is enrolled in that course -- $152,700."
-- Note: "The HELP loan limit is indexed under Part 5-6." (The current-year limit is an INPUT to the balance below.)
@export What is my HELP loan limit, as s 128-20 states it (before indexation)?
GIVEN `enrolled in medicine, dentistry, veterinary science or aviation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are enrolled in a course in medicine, dentistry, veterinary science or aviation
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my HELP loan limit` IS
    IF `enrolled in medicine, dentistry, veterinary science or aviation` THEN 152700 ELSE 106319

-- s 128-15(1): the HELP balance is (a) if the HELP loan limit "exceeds the sum of all of the amounts of" HECS-HELP, FEE-HELP,
-- VET FEE-HELP and VET student loans "previously payable for the person", that sum "as reduced by any amounts previously
-- re-credited" -- "that excess"; (b) "otherwise -- zero". (2): "it is immaterial whether amounts ... have been repaid."
@export What is my HELP balance (s 128-15)?
GIVEN `HELP loan limit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your HELP loan limit for the year, in dollars
      `assistance previously payable` IS A NUMBER @desc All the HECS-HELP, FEE-HELP, VET FEE-HELP and VET student loan amounts payable for you so far, in dollars
      `amounts re-credited` IS A NUMBER @desc The amounts re-credited to your balance so far, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my HELP balance` IS
    max 0 (`HELP loan limit` MINUS (`assistance previously payable` MINUS `amounts re-credited`))

-- s 128-25(1), (2): if, during "the financial year starting on 1 July 2019" or a later one, "a payment was made in discharge of
-- the whole or a part of a debt" under Chapter 4, the Commissioner notifies it after the year ends and "the Secretary must
-- re-credit the person's HELP balance with an amount equal to the amount of the payment" (Note 1: "The payment may be a
-- voluntary repayment."). (2A), (2B): the amounts cut by ss 137-19A and 140-26 are re-credited too.
@export By how much will my HELP balance be re-credited for a financial year (s 128-25)?
GIVEN `financial year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year starts (2024 for 2024-25)
      `payments in discharge of my HELP debts in that year` IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid off your HELP debts that year, voluntarily or compulsorily, in dollars
      `amounts cut by the 20 per cent reductions` IS A NUMBER @desc The amounts taken off your debts by the 2025 20% cut (ss 137-19A, 140-26), in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how much is my HELP balance re-credited` IS
    (IF `financial year starting in` AT LEAST 2019 THEN `payments in discharge of my HELP debts in that year` ELSE 0)
        PLUS `amounts cut by the 20 per cent reductions`

§§ `ss 137-5, 137-10, 137-19A -- What becomes a HELP debt`

-- s 137-5(3) and s 137-10(3): a HECS-HELP or FEE-HELP debt "is taken to have been incurred by a person immediately after the
-- census date for the unit". s 137-19A: "(1) This section applies if ... a person incurs a HELP debt during the period beginning on
-- 1 January 2025 and ending on 1 June 2025. (2) ... the amount of the HELP debt is the amount worked out under that section reduced
-- by 20%." INFERENCE: "immediately after the census date" is read as the day after it -- so a census date of 31 December 2024
-- falls inside the window and one of 1 June 2025 falls outside it.
@export Is my HELP debt for the unit cut by 20% because it was incurred between 1 January and 1 June 2025 (s 137-19A)?
GIVEN `the census day` IS A NUMBER @desc The unit's census date, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my HELP debt for the unit cut by 20 per cent` IF
    `the census day` AT LEAST 20241231 AND `the census day` AT MOST 20250531

-- s 137-5(2): "The amount of the HECS-HELP debt is the amount of the loan." Then s 137-19A.
@export What HECS-HELP debt do I incur for the unit (ss 137-5, 137-19A)?
GIVEN `loan` IS A NUMBER @desc The HECS-HELP assistance lent to you for the unit, in dollars
      `the census day` IS A NUMBER @desc The unit's census date, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What HECS-HELP debt do I incur for the unit` IS
    IF `Is my HELP debt for the unit cut by 20 per cent` `the census day`
    THEN `loan` TIMES 80 DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE `loan`

-- s 137-10(2): the FEE-HELP debt is "(a) if the loan relates to FEE-HELP assistance for a unit of study provided by a Table B
-- provider -- the amount of the loan; or (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply and the loan relates to FEE-HELP assistance for a unit
-- of study that forms part of an undergraduate course of study: (i) for a unit of study with a census date between 1 April 2020
-- and 31 December 2022 -- the amount of the loan; or (ia) for a unit of study with a census date on or after 1 January 2023 -- an
-- amount equal to 120% of the loan; or (ii) otherwise -- an amount equal to 125% of the loan; or (c) if neither paragraph (a) nor
-- (b) applies -- the amount of the loan." Then s 137-19A.
@export What FEE-HELP debt do I incur for the unit, including any loan fee (ss 137-10, 137-19A)?
GIVEN `loan` IS A NUMBER @desc The FEE-HELP assistance lent to you for the unit, in dollars
      `Table B unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the unit is provided by a Table B provider
      `undergraduate unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the unit is part of an undergraduate course of study
      `the census day` IS A NUMBER @desc The unit's census date, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What FEE-HELP debt do I incur for the unit` IS
    IF `Is my HELP debt for the unit cut by 20 per cent` `the census day`
    THEN `the FEE-HELP debt before s 137-19A` TIMES 80 DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE `the FEE-HELP debt before s 137-19A`
  WHERE
    `the FEE-HELP debt before s 137-19A` MEANS
        IF `Table B unit` OR (NOT `undergraduate unit`) THEN `loan`
        ELSE IF `the census day` AT LEAST 20200401 AND `the census day` AT MOST 20221231 THEN `loan`
             ELSE IF `the census day` AT LEAST 20230101 THEN `loan` TIMES 120 DIVIDED BY 100
                  ELSE `loan` TIMES 125 DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `ss 140-5, 140-10, 140-25, 140-26, 140-30 -- How my debt grows`

-- s 140-10(1)(b): the HELP debt indexation factor for 1 June is "the lower of the CPI indexation factor ... and the WPI
-- indexation factor", each a ratio of four quarters' index numbers "rounded to 3 decimal places" (INPUTS, already rounded).
@export What indexation factor applies to my HELP debt on 1 June (s 140-10)?
GIVEN `CPI indexation factor` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPI indexation factor for 1 June, rounded to 3 places
      `WPI indexation factor` IS A NUMBER @desc The WPI indexation factor for 1 June, rounded to 3 places
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What indexation factor applies to my HELP debt` IS
    min `CPI indexation factor` `WPI indexation factor`

-- s 140-5(1): the former accumulated HELP debt is the method statement amount multiplied by the HELP debt indexation factor.
-- Step 1: the previous accumulated HELP debt; Steps 2-2C: add the HELP debts incurred in the last 6 months of the preceding
-- financial year; Step 3: subtract voluntary repayments; Step 4: subtract compulsory repayment amounts assessed; Step 5:
-- subtract increases by amended assessment; Step 6: add reductions by amended assessment. s 140-26(1): for the accumulated HELP
-- debt for the financial year starting on 1 July 2024 add "Step 7. Reduce the amount worked out under step 6 by 20%."
-- The Act's example: Lorraine, $15,000 + $1,500 - $525 - $3,000, at a factor of 1.030.
@export What is my former accumulated HELP debt (ss 140-5, 140-26(1))?
GIVEN `previous accumulated HELP debt` IS A NUMBER @desc Your accumulated HELP debt on the previous 1 June, in dollars
      `HELP debts in the last 6 months` IS A NUMBER @desc HELP debts you incurred in the last 6 months of the preceding financial year, in dollars
      `voluntary repayments` IS A NUMBER @desc Voluntary repayments made in the period, in dollars
      `compulsory repayments assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc Compulsory repayment amounts assessed in the period, in dollars
      `increases by amendment` IS A NUMBER @desc Increases in compulsory repayments by amended assessment, in dollars
      `reductions by amendment` IS A NUMBER @desc Reductions in compulsory repayments by amended assessment, in dollars
      `indexation factor` IS A NUMBER @desc The HELP debt indexation factor for 1 June
      `the financial year starts on 1 July 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the accumulated debt for the financial year starting 1 July 2024
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my former accumulated HELP debt` IS
    (`previous accumulated HELP debt` PLUS `HELP debts in the last 6 months` MINUS `voluntary repayments`
        MINUS `compulsory repayments assessed` MINUS `increases by amendment` PLUS `reductions by amendment`)
    TIMES (IF `the financial year starts on 1 July 2024` THEN 80 DIVIDED BY 100 ELSE 1)
    TIMES `indexation factor`

-- s 140-25(1), formula (sidecar): Former accumulated HELP debt + HELP debts incurred - HELP debt repayments - Location-preferred
-- HELP debtor reduction. "HELP debt repayments" are voluntary repayments of the HELP debts incurred in the year; "HELP debts
-- incurred" are those incurred in the first 6 months of the financial year (s 140-25(1A)). The Act's example (Paula: $20,000 +
-- $1,500 = $21,500) agrees.
-- s 140-30: "disregard the number of cents"; under one dollar "is taken to be zero". s 140-25(2): incurred on 1 June.
@export What is my accumulated HELP debt on 1 June (ss 140-25, 140-30)?
GIVEN `former accumulated debt` IS A NUMBER @desc Your former accumulated HELP debt, in dollars
      `HELP debts incurred` IS A NUMBER @desc HELP debts you incurred in the first 6 months of the financial year, in dollars
      `HELP debt repayments` IS A NUMBER @desc Voluntary repayments of those debts before 1 June, in dollars
      `location-preferred reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc Any reduction for location-preferred HELP debtors, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my accumulated HELP debt` IS
    max 0 (FLOOR (`former accumulated debt` PLUS `HELP debts incurred` MINUS `HELP debt repayments` MINUS `location-preferred reduction`))

-- s 140-26(2): for the financial year starting on 1 July 2024 the first s 140-25(1) formula is "omitted and substituted with"
-- (sidecar): Former accumulated HELP debt + [(HELP debts incurred - HELP debt repayments) x 0.8] - Location-preferred HELP
-- debtor reduction. s 140-30 rounding applies as before.
@export What is my accumulated HELP debt on 1 June 2025 (ss 140-25, 140-26(2), 140-30)?
GIVEN `former accumulated debt` IS A NUMBER @desc Your former accumulated HELP debt (already cut by 20% under s 140-26(1)), in dollars
      `HELP debts incurred` IS A NUMBER @desc HELP debts you incurred from 1 July to 31 December 2024, in dollars
      `HELP debt repayments` IS A NUMBER @desc Voluntary repayments of those debts before 1 June 2025, in dollars
      `location-preferred reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc Any reduction for location-preferred HELP debtors, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my accumulated HELP debt on 1 June 2025` IS
    max 0 (FLOOR (`former accumulated debt` PLUS ((`HELP debts incurred` MINUS `HELP debt repayments`) TIMES 8 DIVIDED BY 10)
                  MINUS `location-preferred reduction`))

§§ `ss 151-1, 151-10, 151-15 -- Paying it off early`

-- s 151-1: "(1) A person may at any time make a payment in respect of a debt that the person owes to the Commonwealth under this
-- Chapter. (2) The payment must be made to the Commissioner." There is no minimum and no condition: the answer is yes.
@export May I make a voluntary repayment of my HELP debt (s 151-1)?
GIVEN `I owe a HELP debt or accumulated HELP debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you owe the Commonwealth a HELP debt or accumulated HELP debt
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make a voluntary repayment` IF `I owe a HELP debt or accumulated HELP debt`

-- s 151-10: "(1) ... applied in payment of those debts as the person directs at the time of the payment. (2) If the person has
-- not given any directions, or the directions given do not adequately deal with the matter, any money available is to be applied
-- as follows: (a) first, in discharge or reduction of any accumulated HELP debt of the person; (b) secondly, in discharge or
-- reduction of ... any HELP debt of the person ... in the order in which they were incurred." Without directions:
@export Without directions, how much of my voluntary repayment goes to my accumulated HELP debt (s 151-10(2)(a))?
GIVEN `payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you pay, in dollars
      `accumulated HELP debt` IS A NUMBER @desc Your accumulated HELP debt, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my repayment goes to my accumulated HELP debt` IS
    min `payment` `accumulated HELP debt`

@export Without directions, how much of my voluntary repayment goes to my HELP debts not yet accumulated (s 151-10(2)(b))?
GIVEN `payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you pay, in dollars
      `accumulated HELP debt` IS A NUMBER @desc Your accumulated HELP debt, in dollars
      `other HELP debts` IS A NUMBER @desc HELP debts incurred since the last 1 June, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my repayment goes to my newer HELP debts` IS
    min (`payment` MINUS `How much of my repayment goes to my accumulated HELP debt` `payment` `accumulated HELP debt`) `other HELP debts`

-- s 151-15: if the amount paid "exceeds the sum of: (i) the amount required to discharge the total debt that the person owed to the
-- Commonwealth under this Chapter; and (ii) the total amount of the person's primary tax debts ...; the Commonwealth must refund
-- to the person an amount equal to that excess."
@export How much of my voluntary repayment must be refunded to me (s 151-15)?
GIVEN `payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you pay, in dollars
      `total HELP debt` IS A NUMBER @desc Everything you owe under Chapter 4 (accumulated and newer HELP debts), in dollars
      `primary tax debts` IS A NUMBER @desc Your primary tax debts, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my repayment is refunded to me` IS
    max 0 (`payment` MINUS (`total HELP debt` PLUS `primary tax debts`))

§§ `ss 154-1 to 154-25 -- When must I repay, and how much`

-- s 154-5(1): repayment income is the sum of "(a) the person's taxable income for the income year, disregarding the person's
-- assessable FHSS released amount ...; (b) the person's total net investment loss ...; (c) [if an employee] the reportable fringe
-- benefits total ...; (d) the person's exempt foreign income ...; (e) the person's reportable superannuation contributions".
@export What is my repayment income for the income year (s 154-5)?
GIVEN `taxable income less FHSS released amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable income, leaving out any FHSS released amount, in dollars
      `total net investment loss` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total net investment loss, in dollars
      `reportable fringe benefits total` IS A NUMBER @desc Your reportable fringe benefits total, in dollars
      `exempt foreign income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your exempt foreign income, in dollars
      `reportable superannuation contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc Your reportable superannuation contributions, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my repayment income` IS
    `taxable income less FHSS released amount` PLUS `total net investment loss` PLUS `reportable fringe benefits total`
        PLUS `exempt foreign income` PLUS `reportable superannuation contributions`

-- s 154-10: "The minimum repayment income for an income year is $67,000." s 154-20(2): 15% between the minimum and "$125,000",
-- 17% above. s 154-25(2): each is replaced by an indexed amount "At the start of each income year ... after the 2025-26 income
-- year". INFERENCE: ss 154-10 and 154-20 were substituted ("rs No 30, 2025", endnotes) by the Universities Accord (Cutting Student
-- Debt by 20 Per Cent) Act 2025; read with s 154-25(2), the compiled text speaks to 2025-26 onward. Earlier years ran on a repealed
-- text that is not deposited.
DECLARE `Repayment thresholds` IS ONE OF
    `the thresholds the compiled text states`
    `thresholds indexed under s 154-25, not stated in the text`
    `a repealed rule that is not in the deposit`

@export Which repayment thresholds does the deposited text give for my income year (ss 154-10, 154-20, 154-25)?
GIVEN `income year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year starts (2025 for 2025-26)
GIVETH A `Repayment thresholds`
DECIDE `Which repayment thresholds apply to my income year` IS
    IF `income year starting in` EQUALS 2025 THEN `the thresholds the compiled text states`
    ELSE IF `income year starting in` GREATER THAN 2025 THEN `thresholds indexed under s 154-25, not stated in the text`
         ELSE `a repealed rule that is not in the deposit`

-- The minimum repayment income: $67,000 for 2025-26; the indexed figure (an INPUT) after that; NOTHING before 2025-26, because
-- the deposited text does not say what it was.
-- s 154-25(2), formula (sidecar): Indexable amount for the 2025-26 income year x (AWE for the indexation year / AWE for the
-- 2025-26 income year). (3): dollars and cents are rounded "down to the nearest dollar". AWE (the sum of two quarterly average
-- weekly earnings figures) is published by the Australian Statistician and is an INPUT.
@export What does an indexable amount become in an indexation year after 2025-26 (s 154-25(2), (3))?
GIVEN `indexable amount for 2025-26` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount for 2025-26: $67,000 minimum repayment income or $125,000 upper threshold
      `AWE for the indexation year` IS A NUMBER @desc AWE for the indexation year (s 154-25(2)), in dollars
      `AWE for 2025-26` IS A NUMBER @desc AWE for the 2025-26 income year, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What does an indexable amount become` IS
    FLOOR (`indexable amount for 2025-26` TIMES `AWE for the indexation year` DIVIDED BY `AWE for 2025-26`)

@export What is my minimum repayment income for the income year (ss 154-10, 154-25)?
GIVEN `income year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year starts (2025 for 2025-26)
      `indexed minimum repayment income` IS A NUMBER @desc For years after 2025-26: the indexed minimum published for the year, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my minimum repayment income` IS
    CONSIDER `Which repayment thresholds apply to my income year` `income year starting in`
    WHEN `the thresholds the compiled text states` THEN JUST 67000
    WHEN `thresholds indexed under s 154-25, not stated in the text` THEN JUST `indexed minimum repayment income`
    WHEN `a repealed rule that is not in the deposit` THEN NOTHING

-- s 154-1(1): a person is liable if "(a) the person's repayment income for an income year exceeds the minimum repayment income
-- for the income year; and (b) on 1 June immediately preceding the making of an assessment ... the person had an accumulated HELP
-- debt". (2): "not liable ... if, under section 8 of the Medicare Levy Act 1986: (a) no Medicare levy is payable by the person ...;
-- or (b) the amount of the Medicare levy payable ... is reduced." (s 8 is not deposited: asked as facts.)
@export Must I make a compulsory HELP repayment for the income year (s 154-1)?
GIVEN `repayment income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your repayment income for the income year, in dollars
      `minimum repayment income` IS A NUMBER @desc The minimum repayment income for the income year, in dollars
      `had an accumulated HELP debt on the preceding 1 June` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had an accumulated HELP debt on the 1 June before your assessment
      `no Medicare levy payable under s 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, under s 8 of the Medicare Levy Act 1986, you pay no Medicare levy
      `Medicare levy reduced under s 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, under s 8 of the Medicare Levy Act 1986, your Medicare levy is reduced
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I make a compulsory repayment` IF
        `repayment income` GREATER THAN `minimum repayment income`
    AND `had an accumulated HELP debt on the preceding 1 June`
    AND (NOT `no Medicare levy payable under s 8`)
    AND (NOT `Medicare levy reduced under s 8`)

-- s 154-15(1): the repayable debt is the accumulated HELP debt, or "the amount (if any) remaining after deducting from that debt"
-- amounts paid in reduction of it or assessed under s 154-35 to be payable.
@export What is my repayable debt for the income year (s 154-15)?
GIVEN `accumulated debt` IS A NUMBER @desc Your accumulated HELP debt on the 1 June before your assessment, in dollars
      `amounts paid or assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc Amounts already paid off it or assessed as payable, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my repayable debt` IS
    max 0 (`accumulated debt` MINUS `amounts paid or assessed`)

-- s 154-20(1): the amount is "the least of the following: (a) the amount worked out under subsection (2); (b) the amount equal to
-- 10% of the person's repayment income for the income year; (c) the amount of the person's repayable debt". (2): "(a) 15% of the
-- part of the person's repayment income that exceeds the minimum repayment income but does not exceed $125,000; (b) 17% of the
-- part of the person's repayment income that exceeds $125,000." The rates are a table of two bands, as data:
DECLARE `Repayment band` HAS
    `from` IS A NUMBER
    `to` IS A NUMBER
    `rate per cent` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `minimum repayment income` IS A NUMBER
      `upper threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Repayment band`
`the s 154-20(2) bands` MEANS
    LIST `Repayment band` `minimum repayment income` `upper threshold` 15
       , `Repayment band` `upper threshold` 1000000000000 17

GIVEN `repayment income` IS A NUMBER
      `band` IS A `Repayment band`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the repayment in the band` MEANS
    max 0 ((min `repayment income` (`band`'s `to`)) MINUS `band`'s `from`) TIMES `band`'s `rate per cent` DIVIDED BY 100

@export How much is my compulsory HELP repayment for the income year (s 154-20)?
GIVEN `repayment income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your repayment income for the income year, in dollars
      `minimum repayment income` IS A NUMBER @desc The minimum repayment income for the year ($67,000 for 2025-26), in dollars
      `upper threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 154-20(2) upper threshold for the year ($125,000 for 2025-26), in dollars
      `repayable debt` IS A NUMBER @desc Your repayable debt for the income year, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my compulsory repayment` IS
    min (min `the marginal amount` (`repayment income` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100)) `repayable debt`
  WHERE
    `the marginal amount` MEANS
        sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD `the repayment in the band` `repayment income` b) (`the s 154-20(2) bands` `minimum repayment income` `upper threshold`))

§§ `ss 137-20, 140-40 -- What happens to the debt if I die`

-- s 137-20: "Upon the death of a person who owes a HELP debt to the Commonwealth, the debt is taken to have been paid."
-- s 140-40: "(1) Upon the death of a person who has an accumulated HELP debt, the accumulated HELP debt is taken to be discharged.
-- (2) To avoid doubt, this section does not affect any compulsory repayment amounts required to be paid in respect of the
-- accumulated HELP debt, whether or not those amounts were assessed before the person's death."
@export If I die, how much of my HELP debts can still be collected (ss 137-20, 140-40)?
GIVEN `accumulated HELP debt` IS A NUMBER @desc Your accumulated HELP debt at death, in dollars
      `HELP debts not yet accumulated` IS A NUMBER @desc HELP debts incurred since the last 1 June, in dollars
      `compulsory repayment amounts owing` IS A NUMBER @desc Compulsory repayment amounts owing for income years before death, assessed or not, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `If I die how much of my HELP debts can still be collected` IS
    `compulsory repayment amounts owing`

§§ `s 154-18(1) -- Leaving Australia`

-- s 154-18(1): a person who "(a) has an accumulated HELP debt or otherwise has a HELP debt that has not yet been discharged; and
-- (b) leaves Australia (other than in circumstances specified in the Overseas Debtors Repayment Guidelines) with the intention of
-- remaining outside Australia for at least 183 days; must, no later than 7 days after leaving Australia, give a notice to the
-- Commissioner in the approved form." The Guidelines are not deposited: whether they except you is asked as a fact.
@export Must I notify the Commissioner of Taxation that I have left Australia (s 154-18(1))?
GIVEN `have an undischarged HELP debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an accumulated HELP debt or another undischarged HELP debt
      `left intending to stay away at least 183 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you left Australia intending to stay outside it for at least 183 days
      `excepted by the Overseas Debtors Repayment Guidelines` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Overseas Debtors Repayment Guidelines except your circumstances
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I notify the Commissioner that I have left Australia` IF
        `have an undischarged HELP debt`
    AND `left intending to stay away at least 183 days`
    AND (NOT `excepted by the Overseas Debtors Repayment Guidelines`)

@export Within how many days after leaving Australia must I notify the Commissioner (s 154-18(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days after leaving must I notify the Commissioner` IS 7
